      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Undershore [zone=295]\n**Who:**\n- an old shiliskin fortune teller [npc=19124]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Loot\n**Quest Items:**\n- Fractured Bone Ridges [item=45607]\n- Fractured Frontal Plate [item=50759]\n- Fractured Temporal Plate [item=45605]\n- Fractured Werewolf Incisors [item=45608]\n- Fractured Werewolf Jawbone [item=45604]\n- Funeral Shroud of Den Lord Rakban [item=45606]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Corathus Creep [zone=294]\n- Ruins of Illsalin [zone=298]\n- Snarlstone Dens: Confronting a Traitor [zone=296]\n- Stoneroot Falls [zone=297]\n- The Hive [zone=304]\n**Related Quests:**\n- DoD Level 69 Spell #1: The Lost Notebook [quest=3204]\n- DoD Level 69 Spell #2: Cavern Botany [quest=3223]\n- DoD Level 69 Spell #3: The Search for Clues [quest=3225]\n- DoD Level 69 Spell #4: Rescue Cicero! [quest=3226]\n- DoD Level 70 Spell #1: Preemptive Strike [quest=3214]\n- DoD Level 70 Spell #2: Praetorian Guard [quest=3227]\n- DoD Level 70 Spell #3: The Fall of Illsalin [quest=3228]\n- DoD Level 70 Spell #4: Flights of the Seeker [quest=3206]\n- DoD Level 70 Spell #5: Into the Shadows [quest=3215]\n- Elder Longshadow #1: Freeing an Elder [quest=3267]\n- Elder Longshadow #2: The Orb of Subversion [quest=3269]\n- Elder Longshadow #3: A Plea for Help [quest=3268]\n- Elder Longshadow #4: Trailing Longshadow [quest=3270]\n- Elder Longshadow #5: Confronting a Traitor [quest=3286]\n- Find Fibblebrap 1: The Mines [quest=3509]\n- Find Fibblebrap 2: Lost Caverns [quest=3364]\n- Find Fibblebrap 3: The Hive [quest=3363]\n- Find Fibblebrap 4: The Korlach [quest=3510]\n- Find Fibblebrap 5: The Rescue [quest=3511]\n- Korlach Leviathan #1: The Search for Coral [quest=3220]\n- Korlach Leviathan #2: Learning the Power [quest=3356]\n- Korlach Leviathan #3: Discovering the Secret [quest=3357]\n- Korlach Leviathan #4: Taking Control [quest=3358]\n**Era:** | !Depths of Darkhollow\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Nov 15 18:05:29 2005\nModified: Tue Jan 27 03:31:39 2026 | | _\"an old shiliskin fortune teller\" may be found at +1330, -700, -11._\nan old shiliskin fortune teller regards you indifferently -- it appears to be quite formidable.\nYou say, 'Hail, an old shiliskin fortune teller'\nThe shiliskin stands motionless as though lost in thought. Finally, he speaks, 'Strange things I have seen in these pools, surface dweller. The future, the past, images of warfare. . . it all swirls together here in these [waters].'\nYou say, 'Waters?'\nan old shiliskin fortune teller says 'These waters mark the gravesite of Den Lord Rakban, a werewolf demigod that was Wuria's mate. Wuria blessed her companion with unnatural strength so he could lead the werewolves against the shilsikin long before our empire was formed. After decades of bloodshed, my ancestors lured Rakban into this blind canyon where we now stand. Our korlach priests summoned a tidal wave and drowned Rakban and his warriors forever. There are however, [things] in this world that no amount of water can wash away.'\nYou say, 'What things?'\nan old shiliskin fortune teller says 'The spirit of Den Lord Rakban lingers still. He waits for a worthy warrior so that he may manifest his power once again. Before anyone can confront the spirit, they must first [master the dangers] of Darkhollow. Only then will Rakban return from the spirit world.'\nYou say, 'I will master the dangers.'\nan old shiliskin fortune teller says 'You think you are ready? Very well, return to me when you have completed a great feat in each of the main caverns of Darkhollow. Only then can I stir the waters to summon the spirit.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Depths of Darkhollow'.\nTo invoke the spirit of the werewolf Demigod Rakban, you must complete a dangerous feat in each of the main caverns of Darkhollow. Only then will the spirit manifest for you. Venture out and complete these dangerous feats. Return to the shillskin Fortune Teller when you are successful with each one and he will attempt to call the spirit of Den Lord Rakban.\n_This is a five-part task, where you must complete each of five quest lines and come back and finish this afterward. You can start this task before or after you've finished the five quest lines._\n\n---\n\nFind Fibblebrap in the Creep of Corathus 0/1 (Corathus Creep)\n_Bellfast in Corathus Creep is the task-giver, once you have high amiable faction with Expedition 328._\n_Complete the five \"Find Fibblebrap\" tasks in order._\n_The reward is a +50 to fire (Aura of Burning Arcanum) instant click item: Fractured Werewolf Jawbone_\n\n---\n\nLearn the fate of Elder Longshadow in Undershore 0/1 (Undershore)\n_Shadowalker Dustspirit in Stoneroot Falls is the task-giver._\n_Complete the five \"Elder Longshadow\" tasks in order. After you've done so:_\nYou say, 'Hail, an old shiliskin fortune teller'\nYour task 'The Depths of Darkhollow' has been updated.\nA chorus of wolf howls echo strangely off the cavern walls. When you look towards the direction of the last echo, you see a small wolf skull fragment resting on a nearby ledge. The shiliskin fortune teller speaks. 'Rakban's spirit knows of your assistance to the Ragepaw werewolves in Undershore. The demigod's spirit is pleased and has rewarded you with power.'\n_The reward is a +50 to cold (Aura of Freezing Arcanum) instant click item: Fractured Temporal Plate_\n\n---\n\nSurvive the Korlach Leviathan Below Stoneroot Falls 0/1 (Stoneroot Falls)\n_Widdlethorpe Gemfinder in Stoneroot Falls is the task-giver._\n_Complete the four group \"Korlach\" tasks in order, the raid is not necessary._\n_The reward is a +50 to magic (Aura of Chromatic Arcanum) instant click item. Fractured Frontal Plate_\n\n---\n\nFulfill Jarzarrad's Prophecy in The Ruins of Illsalin (0/1) - Ruins of Illsalin\n_Jarzarrad the Prophet in Undershore is the task giver._\n_Complete the five \"DoD Level 70 Spell\" tasks in order. After you have completed the tasks:_\nYou say, 'Hail, an old shiliskin fortune teller'\nYour task 'The Depths of Darkhollow' has been updated.\nAn uneasy sensation clouds your mind, as though you suspect you are being watched or hunted. Suddenly watchful, you discover a shard of a wolf skull that has drifted ashore near your feet. The shiliskin fortune teller nods at the shard. 'Take it,' he says. 'The demigod Rakban knows your fulfillment of Jarzarrad's prophecy and has chosen to reward you with a fragment of power.'\n_The reward is a +50 to poison (Aura of Venomous Arcanum) instant click item: Fractured Bone Ridges_\n\n---\n\nRescue the Ecologist of Expedition 328 from The Hive (0/1) - The Hive\n_Brovil Pallivineg in Corathus Creep is the task giver._\n_Complete the five \"DoD Level 69 Spell\" tasks in order. After you have completed the tasks:_\nYou say, 'Hail, an old shiliskin fortune teller'\nYour task 'The Depths of Darkhollow' has been updated.\nA flicking movement in the water catches your eye. You think you see a reflection of a giant wolf watching you from the pool's edge, but the image vanishes as soon as your eyes settle on it. In its place is a bone fragment about the size of dagger. 'Take it,' the shiliskin fortune teller says. 'Rakban's spirit wants you to have it.'\n_The reward is a +50 to disease (Aura of Blight Arcanum) instant click item: Fractured Werewolf Incisors_\n\n---\n\n(opt) Wrap all werewolf skull fragments in the funeral shroud of den lord Rakban (0/1) - ALL\nCompletion of each quest line gives you an insta-click resist item that adds 50 to the associated resist. They are part of a werewolf head, and are to be combined in the container provided (Funeral Shroud of Den Lord Rakban) when all the tasks are complete to create \"Ancient Werewolf Skull\".\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Ancient Werewolf Skull.\nThe final reward is a +50 to all resists (Aura of Pure Arcanum) instant click mask, the Ancient Werewolf Skull, which evolves into The Skull of Den Lord Rakban.\nIf you have your lvl 69 and 70 spells/disciplines, hail the fortune teller after receiving this task and you'll get rewards 4 and 5 respectively. You may have to hail more than once to get all the rewards that you are entitled to.\n**Submitted by:** WyreWintermute\n- Ancient Werewolf Skull [item=45603]\n- Fractured Bone Ridges [item=45607]\n- Fractured Frontal Plate [item=50759]\n- Fractured Temporal Plate [item=45605]\n- Fractured Werewolf Incisors [item=45608]\n- Fractured Werewolf Jawbone [item=45604]\n- Skull of the Den Lord [item=45649]\n- The Skull of Den Lord Rakban [item=45602]",
